  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Ulti. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Ulti is a complex 3-player Hungarian card game using a 32-card Hungarian deck. One player (declarer) bids and plays against two defenders. Key bids: Ulti (win last trick with trump 7), Betli (win no tricks), Durchmars (win all tricks). Features talon discard, combinable bids, kontras, and csendes (silent) bonuses.',
    objective: 'The highest bidder becomes declarer and plays alone against the other two. The declarer must fulfill the contracted bid (e.g. score more card points than the defenders, win the last trick with the trump 7 in Ulti, take no tricks in Betli, or take all tricks in Durchmars). The defenders aim to prevent the declarer from fulfilling the contract.',
    gameplay: 'Bid: Passz(1), Ulti(4), 40-100(4), Betli(5), Durchmars(7), 20-100(8). Bids combinable. Kontra doubles stakes. Follow suit, must head, must trump. Last trick = 10 bonus. Silent achievements = half value.',
